1
00:00:00,222 --> 00:00:01,222
Hello!

2
00:00:01,222 --> 00:00:02,758
This is a quick announcement.

3
00:00:02,758 --> 00:00:06,416
The Stop Killing Games campaign
has just launched an official Discord

4
00:00:06,416 --> 00:00:08,005
and it's open to the public.

5
00:00:08,005 --> 00:00:11,685
So if you want to talk more about
the campaign or brainstorm ideas for it,

6
00:00:11,685 --> 00:00:14,236
this is probably the
best place to do so.

7
00:00:14,236 --> 00:00:15,381
Now, I'm the first to admit

8
00:00:15,381 --> 00:00:17,803
this is something we should have
done a long time ago,

9
00:00:17,803 --> 00:00:21,437
and to be fair, we've tried
as far back as April,

10
00:00:21,437 --> 00:00:23,681
but each time, there were complications.

11
00:00:23,681 --> 00:00:25,711
But that may have been
a blessing in disguise,

12
00:00:25,711 --> 00:00:28,343
because this time,
it's being done right

13
00:00:28,343 --> 00:00:29,981
I think.

14
00:00:29,981 --> 00:00:32,183
This one is going to
be well moderated,

15
00:00:32,183 --> 00:00:34,740
run by people with lots
of Discord experience,

16
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:36,394
and support multiple languages,

17
00:00:36,394 --> 00:00:39,140
which is important
for this campaign.

18
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:43,210
Anyway, "better late than never"
is becoming the story of my life.

19
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:46,340
And since we haven't had a
public Discord for the campaign,

20
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:49,365
some unofficial ones have
popped up in the meantime.

21
00:00:49,365 --> 00:00:51,819
That's okay, but we
have no control over those,

22
00:00:51,819 --> 00:00:54,486
and we wanted to make sure
moderation was pretty good

23
00:00:54,486 --> 00:00:56,746
before we publicly endorsed anything,

24
00:00:56,746 --> 00:00:59,200
hence why we're
launching the official one.

25
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,660
So a link to the official one
is in the description of this video,

26
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:05,760
or on the website
StopKillingGames.com.

27
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,270
If it's not one of those links,

28
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:10,798
then it may not be the right one,
and we're not involved with it.

29
00:01:10,798 --> 00:01:12,905
So what is this Discord for?

30
00:01:12,905 --> 00:01:14,840
Well, that's kind of up to you.

31
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:19,030
I want people to be able to organize and
act independently on Stop Killing Games,

32
00:01:19,030 --> 00:01:22,080
and I think this Discord
could facilitate that.

33
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:26,015
That said, there are a couple
clear things I think people can help with.

34
00:01:26,015 --> 00:01:27,256
As a quick refresher,

35
00:01:27,256 --> 00:01:30,635
the Stop Killing Games campaign
is about challenging the legality

36
00:01:30,635 --> 00:01:34,600
of publishers destroying video games
that you've already paid for.

37
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:35,860
Now, over the past year,

38
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:39,160
we've done more on this than I would
have thought possible, really.

39
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:41,980
Here's a quick overview of
everything we've been doing.

40
00:01:41,980 --> 00:01:43,957
Now, some approaches
were dead ends,

41
00:01:43,957 --> 00:01:46,260
but others still show a lot of promise.

42
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:50,630
As someone with no experience
with political activism prior to this,

43
00:01:50,630 --> 00:01:52,790
I think this is damned impressive.

44
00:01:52,790 --> 00:01:55,350
However, most of this
stuff has either concluded,

45
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:58,340
or else we have to wait on
governments before anything will happen.

46
00:01:58,340 --> 00:01:59,888
Out of this list,

47
00:01:59,888 --> 00:02:03,220
these are the remaining options
where we can still do a lot.

48
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:06,205
Everything else is either done
or is a waiting game.

49
00:02:06,205 --> 00:02:09,350
Well, the UK petition
is relaunching.

50
00:02:09,350 --> 00:02:11,715
We submitted it over a month ago.

51
00:02:11,715 --> 00:02:14,310
I honestly thought it
would be open by now.

52
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:17,545
That's going to get its own
promotion once it finally opens.

53
00:02:17,545 --> 00:02:20,870
That's also one thing people can
clearly help spread the word on.

54
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:22,120
Though not yet.

55
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:25,782
Nobody can sign anything right now,
so don't hype it too early.

56
00:02:25,782 --> 00:02:29,160
Now, the European Citizens' Initiative
is more complicated.

57
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:31,517
We have a little over
six months left on that,

58
00:02:31,517 --> 00:02:35,492
but we're only about a third of
where we need to be for that to pass.

59
00:02:35,492 --> 00:02:37,427
And at the time of this video,

60
00:02:37,427 --> 00:02:40,575
the rate we're gathering
signatures is not enough,

61
00:02:40,575 --> 00:02:42,892
and we won't make it
without a big promotion.

62
00:02:42,892 --> 00:02:47,540
That said, we have a big promotion
coming up that I can't talk about yet,

63
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:51,468
and personally, I think it's going
to make or break the initiative.

64
00:02:51,468 --> 00:02:53,747
See, the biggest problem
we've had with the initiative

65
00:02:53,747 --> 00:02:56,390
is simply making
people aware it exists.

66
00:02:56,390 --> 00:02:59,110
Especially non-English speakers.

67
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:02,993
That's a challenge since most of
my audience only speaks English.

68
00:03:02,993 --> 00:03:05,110
Now, I've tried to
get attention on this.

69
00:03:05,110 --> 00:03:07,299
I must have reached
out to maybe...

70
00:03:07,299 --> 00:03:11,620
one or two hundred YouTubers,
streamers, and organizations.

71
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:15,670
And the vast, vast
majority never respond.

72
00:03:15,670 --> 00:03:18,570
So I am not the best
for outreach on this.

73
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:20,872
In fact, I think we're
approaching the limits

74
00:03:20,872 --> 00:03:23,680
of what I'm able to
influence on the campaign.

75
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:27,222
Especially because signatures
are not YouTube views.

76
00:03:27,222 --> 00:03:30,730
I could make another video on this,
and it would barely move the needle,

77
00:03:30,730 --> 00:03:33,190
because people
can only sign once.

78
00:03:33,190 --> 00:03:35,159
It would be preaching to the choir.

79
00:03:35,159 --> 00:03:38,492
But now that we have
a multilingual Discord,

80
00:03:38,492 --> 00:03:41,520
maybe the wisdom of the crowds
can do a better job at this.

81
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:43,028
I hope they can.

82
00:03:43,028 --> 00:03:44,960
Now, I'm still available

83
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:47,510
if there's something important
where I can make a difference.

84
00:03:47,510 --> 00:03:49,780
Plus, I don't always
know what will come up.

85
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:50,722
For example:

86
00:03:50,722 --> 00:03:54,760
Contacting the EU Commission
about this was never the original plan,

87
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:57,050
but it fell into our lap,
so we ran with it.

88
00:03:57,050 --> 00:04:00,000
Now, they ended up telling us
that there might be a violation

89
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,230
but we had to go through
the member states on it,

90
00:04:02,230 --> 00:04:04,090
which is what we
were already doing,

91
00:04:04,090 --> 00:04:06,470
so it was really just
running around in circles,

92
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:09,475
but we didn't know that,
and it seemed like a good angle.

93
00:04:09,475 --> 00:04:11,737
Anyway, I still feel like it's insane

94
00:04:11,737 --> 00:04:15,110
that despite this being such a
widespread issue in gaming,

95
00:04:15,110 --> 00:04:17,360
without clear laws governing it,

96
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:19,910
I had to be the one
to spearhead this,

97
00:04:19,910 --> 00:04:22,600
otherwise it felt like nothing
was going to be done on it.

98
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,440
I mean, me.

99
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,920
What the hell?

100
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:27,830
So I would love to have
more people take over.

101
00:04:27,830 --> 00:04:31,008
And this Discord should
be the perfect place to do so.

102
00:04:31,008 --> 00:04:35,325
Finally, I want to end this by saying
even if the Citizens' Initiative fails—

103
00:04:35,325 --> 00:04:40,020
which I'm not calling yet; give it another
month to see where we're at first—

104
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:42,115
it's not the only play we have.

105
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:45,320
I cannot emphasize
enough what a big deal it is,

106
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:49,790
that we got this escalated not at one,
but three different agencies.

107
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:55,110
It's entirely possible we've already
won this, and we just don't know it yet.

108
00:04:55,110 --> 00:04:58,895
Now, it would be a lot nicer if
the Citizens' Initiative passed,

109
00:04:58,895 --> 00:05:01,725
because then I think that would
really seal the deal on this,

110
00:05:01,725 --> 00:05:04,340
but we can only
do what's possible.

111
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:05,800
All right, that's it.

112
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,760
Join the Discord if you want.

